    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-030: Feature-Class Extensions + Skip-Link Hide** - a small, measurement-driven follow-up to ADR-029 that fixes three remaining visible bugs in Wikipedia's first viewport without touching the structural CSS feature set.\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation (2 commits, ~20 lines of code + ~30 lines of tests) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n## Why this reframes the original ADR-030 plan\n\nThe original plan was **position + :checked**. Live visual verification of Wikipedia (session 2026-10-26) plus a diagnostic on the CSS showed:\n\n| Signal | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Rules with position: | 47 (22 relative / 16 absolute / 3 fixed / 2 sticky / 4 important) |\n| Rules with :checked | 14 |\n| :not() support in our matcher | **none** |\n\n**None of the four visible bugs is fixed by honoring position or :checked.** The three layout bugs share the same root cause as ADR-029's main-menu flip: server-shipped vector-feature-* flags that JS flips at desktop load.\n\n**The :checked rules (14 of them) are for future features** - real stateful dropdowns (language, user menu, page tools) that open on click - not for the current bugs, which are dropdown panels rendering inline when they should be hidden.\n\n## What ADR-030 ships\n\n### 1. Extend apply_viewport_feature_classes() to a flip table\n\nAdd vector-feature-page-tools-pinned-disabled -> -enabled at desktop viewport. Same 1120 threshold, same idempotent round-trip semantics as ADR-029's existing main-menu-pinned flip. Refactor from one inline flip to a constexpr FeatureFlip table - extensible without future code duplication.\n\n**Effect:** the Tools-panel hide rule matches. The 687px Tools panel disappears. Page actions Read / View source / View history move from y~4873 to ~y~180. Article intro moves from y=834 to ~y~300.\n\n### 2. Hide the skip link\n\nInject .mw-jump-link { display: none } with important into the desktop viewport CSS. The important flag beats the .mw-jump-link:not(:focus) rule (which we can't match anyway - no :not, no :focus).\n\n**Honest note:** this is a workaround. When ADR-031 lands (position: absolute + :not + clip + eventually :focus), the workaround can be removed and the skip link becomes Tab-reachable via the standard visually-hidden pattern.\n\n## The scope split\n\n| ADR | Scope | Ships |\n|---|---|---|\n| **030** (this) | Extend feature-flip table; hide skip link | Largest visible delta for ~20 lines of code |\n| **031** (deferred) | position (absolute/fixed/relative), :checked, :not, clip, z-index | Structural infrastructure for future features |\n\nSame discipline that carried ADR-029: **act on what the measurement says, keep the small change small, give the structural work its own cycle.**\n\n## Expected visible delta\n\nMeasured on Wikipedia at viewport 1774:\n\n| Element | Before ADR-030 | After ADR-030 (expected) |\n|---|---|---|\n| .vector-page-toolbar height | 687 | ~40-60 |\n| Read/View source/View history y | ~4873 | ~180-200 |\n| .vector-body (article intro) y | 834 | ~250-350 |\n| Jump to content | visible | hidden |\n| Header height | 36 | 36 (unchanged) |\n| .mw-page-container-inner y | 59 | 59 (unchanged) |\n| Article title visible | yes (y=107) | yes (y=107) |\n\n**Honest caveat**: \"article intro above the fold\" (y<900) requires ADR-031's :checked support to properly collapse the language dropdown (currently hidden by ADR-029's #p-lang-btn workaround). ADR-030 clears 80% of the visible gap - the largest remaining single obstruction (687px).\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Scope split accepted** - ADR-030 is small (feature flip + skip-link hide); structural work defers to ADR-031. Agree with the split?\n- [ ] **#p-lang-btn workaround stays** - still needed until ADR-031's :checked support exists. Confirm.\n- [ ] **Skip-link important workaround** - acceptable as a documented deferral of the full visually-hidden pattern?\n- [ ] **Only page-tools-pinned flipped** - language-in-main-menu-pinned is already correct (-disabled at desktop); clientpref-* flags left alone. Confirm.\n- [ ] **Table refactor** of apply_viewport_feature_classes() - small code-quality improvement bundled with the flip. OK?\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched (spec only). After merge: cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests - expect 394 / 1643 unchanged.\n\n## ADR\n\ndocs/decisions/030-feature-class-extensions.md - Status: Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR. Index row 030 added; reading order bumped to 008 through 030.\n\nRefs #166\n",
